# .claude/PROJECT.md — Example

> This file is created by /init and lives in each project's .claude/ directory.
> It is gitignored — never committed to the project repo.

## Project Configuration

### Stack
Mixed (Next.js + C#/Blazor)

### Project Type
New feature on existing codebase

### Security Sensitivity
Customer-facing
<!-- Options: Internal tool / Customer-facing / Financial or sensitive data -->

### Jira Board
- URL: https://your-team.atlassian.net
- Project: DEV
- Board ID: 309

### Board Mappings
- Features: DEV board 309
- Bugs: DEV board 309
- Incidents: DEV board 309
- Refactors: DEV board 309
- Security: DEV board 309
<!-- These are filled the first time each command type is used -->

### Jira Phase Map
<!--
The phase map tells the toolbox which board column corresponds to each
universal workflow PHASE. Phases are toolbox-internal (Discovery, In Progress,
Code Review, etc.) — column names are per-team Jira UI choices.

This map is the CONTRACT between phases (toolbox concept) and columns (board
reality). It is verified at the start of every /flow run. If a mapped column
no longer exists on the live board, /flow pauses and asks the user to remap
before any phase comments fire.

Semantics:
- Quoted column name → ticket transitions to that column when the phase runs
- null → no column for this phase; comment-only, no transition (the comment
  body gets a prefix like "(in <current_column> — board has no <phase> column)")
- Same column reused across keys → ticket stays put; both phases comment
  in place (natural support for "lump" boards where Code Review happens
  inside In Progress)
- Missing key → phase doesn't execute on this board (defensive — the phase
  is skipped entirely, not silently retargeted)

Set during /init via anchor questions (one per phase) so the user explicitly
states semantic intent ("which column means awaiting human review?"), not
column ordering.
-->
```yaml
jira_phase_map:
  discovery: null                          # board has no Discovery column → comment-only
  ready_for_dev: "Selected for Development"
  in_progress: "In Progress"
  code_review: "In Progress"               # same column reused — review happens inline
  ready_for_release: "Ready for Release"
  done: null                               # human-only; agent rejects phase=done
```

### Jira Board ID
